      "note": "same, through a dial code"
    },
    {
      "country": "IDN",
      "input": "+0062 857 1860 9079",
      "reason": "country_conflict",
      "note": "'+' and '00' are alternative spellings of the same thing, not stackable ones: what follows '+' must be a country code, and '00' is none. This is the one deliberate divergence where the Tracive app accepts the input and these SDKs do not"
    },
    {
      "country": "+62",
      "input": "+0062857 1860 9079",
      "reason": "country_conflict",
      "note": "same, through a dial code"
    },
    {
      "country": "IDN",
      "input": "000",
      "reason": "empty_phone_number",
      "note": "empty once the trunk prefix is stripped. The app folds it to '+62', a key that cannot match anything, so refusing it here is safe"
    },
    {
      "country": "IDN",
      "input": "62",
      "reason": "empty_phone_number",
      "note": "country code only, no subscriber number. The app folds it to '+62'"
    },
    {
      "country": "USA",
      "input": "1",
      "reason": "empty_phone_number",
      "note": "same, NANP trunk prefix"
    },
    {
      "country": "﻿IDN",
      "input": "0857 1860 9079",
      "reason": "unknown_country",
      "note": "a BOM before the country code is refused by all four SDKs. Each platform's own trim() disagreed: Dart and JavaScript strip U+FEFF, Kotlin and Swift do not, so one input behaved two ways"
    },
    {
      "country": "ITA",
      "input": "0000000",
      "reason": "empty_phone_number",
      "note": "a number that is nothing but zeros. Italy does not strip leading zeros, so this used to yield +390000000 — well-formed E.164 that reached the network and was billed for a miss"
    },
    {
      "country": "ITA",
      "input": "+39 0000000",
      "reason": "empty_phone_number",
      "note": "same, already international; the check must run AFTER the country code is stripped"
    },
    {
      "country": "USA",
      "input": "0000000000",
      "reason": "empty_phone_number",
      "note": "NANP does not strip leading zeros either"
    },
    {
      "country": "RUS",
      "input": "00000000000",
      "reason": "empty_phone_number",
      "note": "same for Russia"
    },
    {
      "country": "IDN",
      "input": "0000",
      "reason": "empty_phone_number",
